You're right! The issue is that the CSS is forcing no gaps at a higher level. Let me provide the CSS fixes you need:

Add this CSS to your <style> section (around line 260, before the closing </style> tag):

```css
/* Fix for health chart filter gaps */
.main-content .d-flex.gap-3 {
    gap: 1rem !important;
}

.main-content .vr {
    display: inline-block;
    align-self: stretch;
    width: 1px;
    min-height: 1em;
    background-color: currentColor;
    opacity: 0.25;
    margin: 0 0.25rem;
}

/* Ensure proper spacing between filter elements */
#dashboardHealthFilter,
.btn-group,
#chartModeIndicator {
    margin: 0;
}

.main-content .flex-wrap .btn-group {
    margin: 0 0.25rem;
}

/* Add spacing specifically for the info badge */
#chartModeIndicator .badge {
    margin-left: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
}

/* Alternative: Add margin to the info container */
.main-content .flex-grow-1 {
    margin-left: 0.5rem;
}

/* Ensure the info text has proper spacing */
#chartModeIndicator {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    white-space: nowrap;
}

/* Responsive adjustments */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
    .main-content .d-flex.gap-3 {
        gap: 0.75rem !important;
    }
    
    #chartModeIndicator {
        white-space: normal;
    }
}
```

If that doesn't work, add this more specific override at the end of your CSS:

```css
